From ad1ca8dbbbc32cd6cf97378f9ede9b2dd010a7fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cdiogo1979 <cdiogo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:21:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Use the platform's Spark session; declared task arguments
 and Jupyter widgets

The lakehouse platform now owns the Spark session (catalogs, token source,
redaction) in its lakehouse_spark module. start_spark_job loads this
repository's config and asks the platform for the session with its
catalog_name; the legacy config-dir branches are gone.

notebooks/common/cli.py gains parse_task_args: a job declares its task
arguments once; values come from the workflow's args in Airflow and from
input widgets (jupyter_input_widget_helper.py) or TASK_ARGS in Jupyter.
Values are strings; jobs check them. jupyter_helper.py becomes
notebooks/common/jupyter_environment_resolver.py, which honours
LAKEHOUSE_ENVIRONMENT. generate_tpch.py uses both; tests and docs follow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
